5. THE ONE DEFECT THIS CAPTURE FOUND, AND HOW IT WAS CLOSED
===============================================================================

Recorded because a clean-clone log that only reports success is not a check.

The first clean-clone attempt at 98f0908 (the tree as every prior Phase 4
card left it) built and passed both suites, but at 9 warnings, all
MSTEST0037 ("Use Assert.HasCount/Assert.IsEmpty instead of
Assert.AreEqual(n, x.Count)"), across ReceivingTests.vb, PurchaseReturnTests
.vb and StockCountTests.vb. This card's own wording is "builds at 0
warnings" - not "builds with only pre-existing warning types" or "0 new
warnings" - so 9 is a genuine miss against the box as written, not a
rounding question.

Fixed at commit 4135d52: nine call sites rewritten from
Assert.AreEqual(count, collection.Count) to Assert.HasCount(count,
collection), and Assert.AreEqual(0, collection.Count) to
Assert.IsEmpty(collection). Assertion behaviour is unchanged - both suites
were rerun locally before committing and stayed green at the same counts
(47/47, 346/346) - this is a mechanical rewrite the analyzer itself names,
not a design change. The clone was then discarded and redone from the fix
commit; this file reports that second, corrected run.

No other defect surfaced. In particular: no MSB3030 recurrence (CARRY-04,
watched since the Phase 3 gate) on this run - one clean-clone run is not
evidence either way and CARRY-04 stays a watch item, not proof it is gone.


